, 2016 to Feb 9, 2017.","setup":"The stock rose about 35% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 5 weeks, peaking at $32.61 and pulling back 16% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Dec 20, 2016 it closed at $26.98, below the base's floor of $27.59, without ever closing above the base high of $32.61. Volume that day was 1.4M shares, 1.02x the prior 10-day average. It kept sliding, down to $20.39, and the chart ends at $21.65.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakdown. The stock built what looked like a base, then broke out of the bottom instead of the top. There was never a breakout to buy. When a base gives way below, the move is to stay out, or get out fast if you bought early."}}